  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{2,4,6,\u2026,100},{1,3,5,\u2026,99}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{2,4,6,\u2026,100},{5,15,25\u2026,95}}$ is not a partition because many elements of $Y$ (such as $1$) do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,\u2026,40},{1,2,3,\u2026,99}}$ is not a partition because many elements (such as $2$) appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{0,1,2,3,\u2026,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains the element $0$ that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- ${\u2205,{1,2,3,\u2026,100}}$ is not a partition because the subset $\u2205$ is empty.",
